    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A complete failure map requires understanding your current logic, but generally, two areas pose the highest risk when moving from proprietary to large language models (LLMs). First, the proprietary engine likely excels at precise, deterministic state tracking, whereas LLMs introduce probabilistic outcomes, which is dangerous for mission-critical workflows. Second, Aethelgard's engine might have domain-specific reasoning or complex constraint satisfaction layers that pure generative AI models struggle to enforce consistently. I recommend auditing any workflow relying on exact adherence to internal state transitions or provable correctness before any migration planning begins.",
